-- title:
--   Monotonicity of the zero-scheme ideal under a module map
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $M$, $M'$ be objects of $X$`.Modules`, the monoidal category of sheaves of modules on $X$ whose unit $\mathbb{1}_{X.\mathrm{Modules}}$ is the structure sheaf. Let $s \colon \mathbb{1}_{X.\mathrm{Modules}} \to M$ be a global section of $M$, presented as a morphism out of the monoidal unit, and let $f \colon M \to M'$ be a morphism of sheaves of modules. For a section $s$ of a module $M$ the project attaches to each open $U \subseteq X$ the coefficient ideal `coeffIdeal s U` of $\Gamma(X,U)$, namely the ideal generated by the range of `coeff s U`, which evaluates the restriction of $s$ to $U$ against morphisms $M|_U \to \mathbb{1}$ of modules on $U$; and `zeroSchemeIdeal s` is the infimum, in $X$`.IdealSheafData`, of all ideal sheaf data $J$ with `coeffIdeal s U` $\le J.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ for every affine open $U$ of $X$. The assertion is the inequality `zeroSchemeIdeal (s ≫ f) ≤ zeroSchemeIdeal s` of ideal sheaf data, i.e. the zero scheme of $s$ is contained in that of $f \circ s$.
--
--   This is the functoriality, in the module, of the zero scheme (vanishing scheme) of a global section: pushing a section forward along a homomorphism can only enlarge its vanishing locus, with no hypothesis of injectivity or invertibility on $f$. It is used to obtain that an isomorphism $f$ leaves the zero-scheme ideal unchanged, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal_comp_eq_of_isIso_monoidalV2`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal_comp_eq_of_isIso_monoidalV2).
